    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.02_typed_legs_and_atlas.sections.04_diagram_inventory_table.concrete_anchor_4#qualitycontrolengineer_reader" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_02_typed_legs_and_atlas_sections_04_diagram_inventory_table_concrete_anchor_4#qualitycontrolengineer_reader silm:hasLongDescription "The QualityControlEngineer_reader is the cross-domain reader: a quality-control engineer at a vet clinic who reads the pullback as the conjunction \"the quality holds AND the procedure was followed\". In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'QualityControlEngineer_reader', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
